Well I pulled nethack 3.1 from the ftp.uu.net usenet/comp.sources.games
directory this morning, spent a couple of hours compiling the game, and
anticipated playing only about an hour or so. Well it is nearlly four hours
later and the game is too addicting to stop! There are a group of us around 
here who after ascending several times with version 3.0j had essentially
stopped playing. Version 3.1 has definitely rekindled the desire to spend
probably way tooooo many hours playing this game.

  Much congratulations to the dev team from a number of us here. Thanks!!!
  ====================

So far things are running VERY smoothly (Sparc IPXs running SunOS 4.1.1) and
the game has a MUCH more interesting twist allowing monsters to really fight
back!!! It is very obvious to us that the dev team not only did a very good
job debugging this software but that they have also come up with many new and
creative ideas. I can see already that quite a bit of nethack 3.0j strategy
will have to be relearned when "simple" monsters such as kobolds and gnomes
start fighting back with items such as wands of fire, lighting, scrolls of
create monster.

Now if I could just get revenge on that gnome who used a wand of lighting to
make my 12th level Wizard's wands explode and take my 80hp character from full
hit points to "you have died".........

